  "overview": "**Codex** is a dark-first design system anchored on `#202122` canvas surfaces with `#f7f7f8` primary ink (15.1:1 contrast) and `#36c` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System Sans` (28px display down to 16px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and hairline `1px` structural borders.\n\nMaintained by **Wikimedia**. Source: published token package (https://doc.wikimedia.org/codex/), package `@wikimedia/codex-design-tokens`. Inventory: **91** colors, **33** typography steps, and **8** documented components (GPL-2.0+ license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 8 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#202122` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#202122` -> `#202122`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#36c` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#202122` (dark) with `#f7f7f8` primary text and `#f7f7f8` secondary labels.\n- Use `#36c` with `#f7f7f8` text (5.0:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System Sans` headings with `System Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#202122` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of dark polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
